# .chezmoiignore
#
# List of patterns that chezmoi should ignore.
# Patterns are relative to the destination directory (usually $HOME), not the source directory (this repository).
# It's interpreted as a template, whether or not it has a .tmpl extension.
#
# NOTE:
# `dir/**/*` ignores all contents recursively, but NOT `dir/` itself (saving you from writing `!dir/`).
# However, to manage a nested file, you MUST STILL explicitly negate (`!`) every intermediate directory in its path (e.g., `!dir/sub/`).
#
# References:
# - https://www.chezmoi.io/reference/special-files/chezmoiignore/
# - https://www.chezmoi.io/user-guide/manage-machine-to-machine-differences/#ignore-files-or-a-directory-on-different-machines

# GLOBAL PATTERNS
**/.DS_Store

